From 550522bd126401944d5f2dff933ea4ebae8934fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:38:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] uboot-airoha: add chainloader for Gemtek XR1710G

The Gemtek XR1710G (Brightspeed XR1710G) runs the same signed AXON
vendor bootloader as the Gemtek W1700K, including its Airoha BMT/BBT
handling, so it needs the same chainloader: the vendor bootloader only
loads this U-Boot from the "chainloader" partition, and all OpenWrt data
lives in UBI, which does its own bad block management.

The parts of the board U-Boot uses (UART, reset button, status LEDs,
SPI-NAND and the flash layout) match the W1700K, so the configuration is
the W1700K one with the names changed, plus:

- CONFIG_PINCONF is replaced by CONFIG_PINCTRL_AIROHA_AN7581, as for the
  AN7581 reference board. The W1700K configuration lacks the pin
  controller driver, so U-Boot finds neither the reset button nor the
  status LEDs there ("LED 'status:red' not found (err=-19)").
- The reset button is read when the chainloader starts. If it is held,
  the blue status LED lights up and the recovery image
  (openwrt-airoha-an7581-gemtek_xr1710g-ubi-initramfs-recovery.itb) is
  booted via TFTP from 192.168.1.254, retrying until a server answers.
  This allows recovery without a serial console. The button has to be
  pressed after power is applied: held at power-on, it makes the AN7581
  boot ROM wait for a UART download instead. The chainloader starts about
  15 s after power-on.
- The default menu entry runs boot_ubi instead of boot_production, so a
  broken production volume falls back to the recovery volume.

Based on the XR1710G chainloader by Kenneth Kasilag.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
