+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] an7581: add uboot chainloader for Gemtek XR1710G
+
+The Gemtek XR1710G ships the same signed AXON vendor bootloader with
+Airoha BMT/BBT handling as the Gemtek W1700K, so it needs the same
+chainloader: the vendor bootloader only ever loads this U-Boot from the
+"chainloader" partition, and everything else lives in UBI.
+
+The board differs from the W1700K only in parts U-Boot does not use, so
+the configuration is a copy of the W1700K one with the names changed.
+
+On top of that:
+
+- CONFIG_PINCONF is replaced by CONFIG_PINCTRL_AIROHA_AN7581, as for
+  the AN7581 reference board. The W1700K configuration lacks the pin
+  controller driver, so the reset button and the status LEDs do not
+  work there.
+- The reset button is read: holding it while the chainloader starts
+  boots the recovery image via TFTP, retrying until a TFTP server
+  answers, so a device can be recovered without a serial console.
+- The default menu entry runs boot_ubi, so a broken production volume
+  falls back to the recovery volume.
+
+Based on the XR1710G chainloader by Kenneth Kasilag.
+
+Signed-off-by: Andrey Korshunov <razor1702@gmail.com>
